{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00430",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.79,
      "end_seconds": 4.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Morning! Make yourself comfortable. What seems to be the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.98,
      "end_seconds": 14.9,
      "duration_seconds": 8.92,
      "text": "Oh, I've been feeling very thirsty, and I wanted to get it checked. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.92,
      "end_seconds": 20.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "When did you first notice it? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.39,
      "end_seconds": 29.58,
      "duration_seconds": 8.19,
      "text": "Oh, uh, it's been three weeks, I'm fairly sure. I took the morning off to come in today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.34,
      "end_seconds": 33.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.86,
      "end_seconds": 40.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.71,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.97,
      "end_seconds": 45.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.42,
      "end_seconds": 46.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Moderate, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.67,
      "end_seconds": 53.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "Yeah, I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 53.46,
      "end_seconds": 58.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.57,
      "end_seconds": 61.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.68,
      "end_seconds": 70.32,
      "duration_seconds": 7.64,
      "text": "There's tiredness as well. Oh, and blurry vision. That's been about the same, two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.01,
      "end_seconds": 73.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.97,
      "end_seconds": 76.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "I'd say severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.71,
      "end_seconds": 80.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Have you been feeling very thirsty at any time before this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.82,
      "end_seconds": 86.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "A bit, last year. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 87.58,
      "end_seconds": 89.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Mm, that's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.63,
      "end_seconds": 94.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any fever or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.46,
      "end_seconds": 105.73,
      "duration_seconds": 10.27,
      "text": "No, no fever, no weight loss. I did have tingling in the feet at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.66,
      "end_seconds": 110.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Okay, have you had any foot sores, abdominal pain or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.94,
      "end_seconds": 117.99,
      "duration_seconds": 6.05,
      "text": "I mean, I haven't had foot sores, abdominal pain or vomiting, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.36,
      "end_seconds": 121.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.13,
      "end_seconds": 124.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Yeah, no, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 125.81,
      "end_seconds": 132.81,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Respiratory rate 14, temperature 36.8, pressure 160 over 103, pulse 91."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.35,
      "end_seconds": 138.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "Okay, noted. What medicines do you take regularly? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.65,
      "end_seconds": 148.5,
      "duration_seconds": 8.85,
      "text": "Oh, uh, it's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a round yellow one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.03,
      "end_seconds": 150.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.69,
      "end_seconds": 166.88,
      "duration_seconds": 12.19,
      "text": "For my sugar, I believe. My husband sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. I take atorvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night for my cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 170.94,
      "end_seconds": 174.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 40 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.44,
      "end_seconds": 180.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.92,
      "end_seconds": 191.09,
      "duration_seconds": 10.17,
      "text": "No, I left it at home. Hydrocortisone cream. I take it when needed for the eczema. I used to take ramipril, but I stopped it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.69,
      "end_seconds": 198.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.11,
      "end_seconds": 207.02,
      "duration_seconds": 7.91,
      "text": "I've, I've had high blood pressure for about ten years now. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.28,
      "end_seconds": 209.21,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.94,
      "end_seconds": 220.64,
      "duration_seconds": 10.7,
      "text": "Um, I've had diabetes for about a year now. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. High cholesterol, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.07,
      "end_seconds": 221.8,
      "duration_seconds": 0.73,
      "text": "Go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.1,
      "end_seconds": 225.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Yeah, I've had eczema for five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.49,
      "end_seconds": 232.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known eczema. We'll keep that in mind today. What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 233.28,
      "end_seconds": 235.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "I don't drink at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.17,
      "end_seconds": 237.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.41,
      "end_seconds": 244.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "Uh, yes, I had cataract surgery on my right eye, last year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.12,
      "end_seconds": 249.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.71,
      "end_seconds": 260.08,
      "duration_seconds": 9.37,
      "text": "Uh, yes, penicillin, it gives me swelling of my face. Dust. I come out in... well, itchy eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.27,
      "end_seconds": 264.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.67,
      "end_seconds": 268.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "Can you lie back for me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.83,
      "end_seconds": 284.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Your feet look fine, no ulcers or sores, and the pulses are palpable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.4,
      "end_seconds": 288.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Turn your head to the side for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.42,
      "end_seconds": 299.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Sensation to the monofilament is reduced on the right foot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.96,
      "end_seconds": 301.66,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.42,
      "end_seconds": 329.72,
      "duration_seconds": 25.3,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. So, based on the history and the examination, it fits best with diabetes that isn't well controlled. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. A urine infection is also on my list. I'd also keep a medication issue in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.52,
      "end_seconds": 332.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.34,
      "end_seconds": 347.44,
      "duration_seconds": 14.1,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now diabetes that isn't well controlled is my leading thought, not anything worse. I'd like to arrange an HbA1c for diabetes control. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 348.94,
      "end_seconds": 352.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "I can book that for Monday at 3:30 pm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.31,
      "end_seconds": 354.13,
      "duration_seconds": 0.82,
      "text": "That's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.23,
      "end_seconds": 372.64,
      "duration_seconds": 17.41,
      "text": "We should do a urine protein test for diabetes. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I'd like you to take glimepiride, 1 milligrams, before breakfast, until we review. You take it by mouth. That's for blood sugar control."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 373.24,
      "end_seconds": 376.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Alright, I'll pick it up today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.29,
      "end_seconds": 402.11,
      "duration_seconds": 24.82,
      "text": "Cut back on sweets, sugary drinks and white rice, and keep to regular meal times. Check your feet every day, and never walk barefoot. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. I'll also refer you to a dietitian."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 404.39,
      "end_seconds": 408.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Right, you know, sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 408.69,
      "end_seconds": 416.36,
      "duration_seconds": 7.67,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 417.32,
      "end_seconds": 418.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 420.38,
      "end_seconds": 427.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.83,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if you vomit repeatedly or become drowsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 428.5,
      "end_seconds": 430.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Okay, um, I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 431.46,
      "end_seconds": 434.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Please come and see me in four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 435.23,
      "end_seconds": 440.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "Okay, so sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 441.5,
      "end_seconds": 445.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Take care, and don't hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 446.09,
      "end_seconds": 450.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Uh, that's all, thank you for your time."
    }
  ]
}